    "__doc": "FIELD -> PHYSICAL QUANTITY. This is the ONLY thing that connects the walk's candidate space to the mechanism graph, and it is knowledge the modeller has that the data does not: `params_actual.pressure_MPa` is a number in a payload until somebody says it measures `bond_pressure`. 🔴 IT IS NOT AN ITEM LIST. Nothing here narrows what the contrast compares - every predicate x field x value the walk touches is a candidate whether it is bound or not, and an unbound candidate simply carries `unknown` in the mechanism column instead of a verdict. That is why a newly translated predicate reaches the screen with zero declarations. Key form: `<predicate>:<dotted field path>`, or the bare path to bind every predicate that carries it. 🔴 THE GAPS ARE HONEST, NOT UNFINISHED: `post_bond_queue_h` (the observation-bias model's only source) was such a gap until the evening of 2026-08-14, when the augmentation lane landed POST_BOND_QUEUE atoms carrying `params_actual.post_bond_queue_h` - the binding below became true the day the field became real, with no code moved, which is the completion criterion demonstrating itself. `stage_particle`, `humidity`, `tape_adhesion_anomaly`, `core_cmp_nonuniform` and `dt_pass_count` are still declared causes with no measuring field; `dt_pass_count` is a PATH feature (count of `transferred` hops) rather than a payload leaf and arrives with R7.",
